35:["$","p",null,{"children":"That's the series to scale on. Three caveats before you copy it into production."}]
36:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Queue depth is a derived series, not a metric the binary emits."}]," No\nmetric name exists that an HPA can target directly. You scale on the recording rule, read\nthrough an external-metrics adapter."]}]
37:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The example alert's window is wrong for autoscaling."}]," The shipped\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"NativeLinkQueueBacklog"}]," alert fires on a queue over 100 sustained for 15\nminutes. That is a correct alert (\"you are chronically undersized\") and a\nterrible autoscaling trigger. An HPA wants a window in the tens of seconds. Use\nthe alert for paging and a much shorter window for scaling."]}]
38:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The repository disagrees with itself about worker utilization."}],"\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge:worker_utilization"}]," is defined one way in\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"deployment-examples/metrics/prometheus-recording-rules.yml"}]," and differently in\nthe inline rules inside ",["$","code",null,{"children":"prometheus-config.yaml"}],", and the Kubernetes alert uses\na third expression. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge:actions_per_worker"}]," is also misnamed; it\nrecords a per-worker sum, not an average. Scale on queue depth, which is\nunambiguous, and treat the utilization series as a dashboard aid rather than a\ncontrol input."]}]
39:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-50/60 text-foreground dark:bg-amber-500/10","role":"alert","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400","aria-hidden":"true","children":"$25:props:children:0:props:children"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"The Redis scheduler backend emits no queue metric"}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"execution.active.count"}]," comes from the in-memory awaited-action store only.\nIf you have moved the scheduler to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_backend"}]," with Redis, the\nsignal this whole page depends on is not being emitted. Confirm which backend\nyou're on before you design an autoscaler around it."]}]]}]]}]
3a:["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"scaling-out","children":"Scaling out"}]
3b:["$","ol",null,{"className":"[&>li]:list-none [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-6 my-8 ml-3 border-l-2 border-border pl-10 [counter-reset:step] [&>li]:relative [&>li]:mb-10 [&>li]:last:mb-0 [&>li]:[counter-increment:step] [&>li]:before:absolute [&>li]:before:left-[-57px] [&>li]:before:top-0 [&>li]:before:flex [&>li]:before:h-8 [&>li]:before:w-8 [&>li]:before:items-center [&>li]:before:justify-center [&>li]:before:rounded-full [&>li]:before:border-2 [&>li]:before:border-border [&>li]:before:bg-background [&>li]:before:content-[counter(step)] [&>li]:before:font-mono [&>li]:before:text-sm [&>li]:before:font-semibold [&>li]:before:text-brand [&>li_ul]:my-2 [&>li_ol]:my-2 [&>li_p]:my-2","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["Set ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_inflight_tasks"}]," explicitly on every worker"]}]," and confirm it took\neffect by watching per-worker action counts during a busy build. Leaving it at\nthe default means the horizontal axis is being tuned against an unbounded\nvertical one, and nothing you measure will be stable."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["Get ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge:queue_depth"}]," onto a dashboard"]}]," and watch it through a normal\nday. You are looking for its shape: how deep it goes at peak, how long it stays\nthere, and how quickly it drains. That shape is what sizing decisions are made\nagainst."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Find your per-worker throughput."}]," With a stable pool size, divide actions\ncompleted by workers by time. This is the number that converts \"the queue is 400\ndeep\" into \"I need N more workers,\" and it is workload-specific enough that\nnobody else's figure helps."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Scale manually first, on a written rule."}]," Something as plain as \"if queue\ndepth exceeds 200 for two minutes, add four workers; if it's under 20 for ten\nminutes, remove two\" is enough. Run it by hand for a week. You will learn more\nabout your build's shape than from any amount of upfront design, and you'll have\nthe thresholds an autoscaler needs."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Then automate that rule."}]," On Kubernetes, an HPA on the external metric backed\nby ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge:queue_depth"}],", plus a cluster autoscaler or Karpenter underneath\nso pods have somewhere to land. Elsewhere, whatever your platform's equivalent\nis. The rule you validated by hand becomes the policy.\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/operate/autoscaling-reference","children":"The reference deployment"}]," is that assembled end\nto end, including the parts the shipped manifests are missing."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Move the fleet to spot capacity once retries are proven."}]," A worker that\ndisappears mid-action has its work requeued with its affinity cleared, so\ninterruption is a cost rather than an incident. Verify that in a staging pool by\nkilling a worker mid-build before you rely on it in production."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Wire the drain endpoint to your interruption notice."}]," For shutdowns you get\nwarning about (spot termination, node upgrades), call the scheduler's admin\nendpoint so the worker finishes what it holds and takes nothing new:"]}],["$","$L1d",null,{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},"tabIndex":"0","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M 6,1 C 4.354992,1 3,2.354992 3,4 v 16 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 12 c 1.645008,0 3,-1.354992 3,-3 V 8 7 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 20.707031,6.2929687 l -5,-5 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 15,1 h -1 z m 0,2 h 7 v 3 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 3 v 11 c 0,0.564129 -0.435871,1 -1,1 H 6 C 5.4358712,21 5,20.564129 5,20 V 4 C 5,3.4358712 5.4358712,3 6,3 Z M 15,3.4140625 18.585937,7 H 16 C 15.435871,7 15,6.5641288 15,6 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" /></svg>","children":"$L52"}],"$L53","$L54","$L55","$L56","$L57"]}]]}]
3c:["$","div",null,{"data-verify-block":"","className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-success/40 bg-success-soft/50 px-5 py-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-foreground","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2.25","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"shrink-0 text-success","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"}]}],"You did it right if"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"[&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2 [&>ul]:my-0","children":["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Queue depth rises under load and returns to near zero afterwards, rather than\nsitting at a floor; a floor means you are permanently undersized."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Adding workers visibly shortens the queue's drain time. If it doesn't, the\nbottleneck is the CAS or the network, not worker count."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Per-action durations stay flat as the pool grows. Durations that climb with\npool size mean the workers are contending for something shared."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Killing a worker mid-build produces retried actions and a successful build,\nnot a failed one."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Scale-in does not coincide with a spike in retried actions. If it does, the\ndrain hook isn't being called."}],"\n"]}]}]]}]
3d:["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-the-repository-actually-ships","children":"What the repository actually ships"}]
3e:["$","p",null,{"children":"Being explicit, because the gap is larger than the docs elsewhere imply."}]
3f:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"deployment-examples/docker-compose/docker-compose-multi-worker.yml"}]}]," defines\nthree worker services. They are copy-pasted and identical apart from a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"WORKER_NAME"}]," and a private data volume each: same config file, same shared\nCAS volume, two CPUs and 2 GB each. It has no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"deploy.replicas"}]," and no\nheterogeneity. A fourth worker means pasting a fourth block."]}]
40:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"deployment-examples/docker-compose/test-multi-worker-simple.json5"}]}]," is a\ngenuinely different pattern worth knowing about: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"three workers inside one\nprocess"}],", as three entries in the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"workers"}]," array of a single config. One\nbinary, one config file, three registrations with the scheduler. It's a useful\nshape for a machine you want to subdivide, and it is not the same thing as three\ncontainers."]}]
41:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"kubernetes/components/worker/worker.yaml"}]}]," sets ",["$","code",null,{"children":"replicas: 3"}],". The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lre-cc"}],"\nand ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lre-rs"}]," overlays patch it to 1. The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"siso-chromium"}]," overlay does not patch\nit, so it inherits 3, which looks unintentional."]}]
42:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["No HorizontalPodAutoscaler, KEDA ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ScaledObject"}],", or VPA exists anywhere in\nthe repository for Forge."]}]," The single HPA in the tree scales the\nOpenTelemetry collector. No heterogeneous-pool example exists in\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config/examples/"}]," either; every shipped worker example is a single\nhomogeneous pool. The autoscaling path on this page is one you assemble from\nstandard Kubernetes parts; the recording rules are the raw material, not a\nfinished artifact."]}]
43:["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"backpressure-when-a-worker-needs-to-stop","children":"Backpressure, when a worker needs to stop"}]
44:["$","p",null,{"children":["One mechanism lets a worker refuse work without being removed:\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_precondition_script"}],". It runs before every action, and a non-zero\nexit produces a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ResourceExhausted"}]," error. The scheduler requeues the action\nwithout counting it as an attempt, and marks the worker ",["$","code",null,{"children":"is_paused"}]," ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"only if\nthat worker still has other actions in flight"}],"; the pause clears as soon as\none of them completes. An idle worker whose script fails is never paused: it\nkeeps its registration and is handed the action again on the next\nmatching pass, and rejects it again."]}]
45:["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-worker/src/local_worker.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-worker/src/local_worker.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-worker/src/local_worker.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"preconditions_met"]}]
46:["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-scheduler/src/api_worker_scheduler.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-scheduler/src/api_worker_scheduler.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-scheduler/src/api_worker_scheduler.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"update_action"]}]
47:["$","p",null,{"children":["This is the hook for host-level conditions the scheduler cannot see: disk\nfilling, a shared license pool exhausted, a GPU in a bad state. It costs a\nprocess spawn per action, so keep the script trivial. And note the\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_"}]," prefix: it is not covered by stability guarantees."]}]
48:["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"heterogeneous-pools","children":"Heterogeneous pools"}]
49:["$","p",null,{"children":["One scheduler can route to pools of different shapes; the mechanism is platform\nproperties, and it is covered in full on\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/platform-properties","children":"platform properties"}],". The scaling point\nis narrower: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"each pool is a separate scaling unit with its own queue-depth\nseries"}],", because ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge:queue_depth"}]," groups by instance and priority, not\nby which pool could serve the work."]}]
4a:["$","p",null,{"children":"If you scale a mixed fleet on one aggregate number, a backlog of GPU actions\nwill scale up your compile pool and change nothing. Either split the recording\nrule by the property that distinguishes the pools, or run a scheduler instance\nper pool. The second is blunter and easier to reason about."}]
4b:["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"when-it-doesnt-work","children":"When it doesn't work"}]
4c:["$","$L58",null,{"children":[["$","$L59",null,{"title":"Queue depth is high but workers are not busy","id":"queue-depth-is-high-but-workers-are-not-busy","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Actions are queued that no worker matches. This is nearly always a platform\nproperty mismatch: an action declaring something no worker advertises, or a\nscheduler key configured as ",["$","code",null,{"children":"priority"}]," (which constrains nothing) when it should\nbe ",["$","code",null,{"children":"exact"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"minimum"}],". Adding workers will not help. Check the scheduler's\nworker-match logging, and see\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/platform-properties","children":"platform properties"}],".\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/operate/troubleshooting#actions-queue-forever-and-workers-sit-idle","children":"Troubleshooting"}],"\nhas the log lines that distinguish \"nothing matches\" from \"everything is busy\",\nand why a bad property ",["$","em",null,{"children":"value"}]," hangs where a bad property ",["$","em",null,{"children":"name"}]," errors."]}]}],["$","$L59",null,{"title":"Adding workers doesn't make builds faster","id":"adding-workers-doesnt-make-builds-faster","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The bottleneck is downstream. Workers pull inputs from and push outputs to the\nCAS, so a saturated CAS or a saturated network means more workers just wait in a\ndifferent place. Check CAS latency as you scale, and check\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"connections_per_endpoint"}]," on the workers' ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store; the default of 1 makes\na single connection the ceiling."]}]}],["$","$L59",null,{"title":"Workers keep being marked dead and their actions requeued","id":"workers-keep-being-marked-dead-and-their-actions-requeued","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_timeout_s"}]," defaults to ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"10 seconds"}],", checked once a second. That is a\nshort leash and it is deliberate (fast detection means fast requeue), but a\nworker whose host is starved for longer than that, or whose network hiccups,\nwill be evicted. If you see churn without actual failures, raise it. The cost\nof raising it is a longer stall before a genuinely dead worker's actions are\nretried. Releases up to 1.7.2 defaulted to 5 seconds and only counted\nheartbeats, so a worker busy reporting results could still be evicted."]}]}],["$","$L59",null,{"title":"Setting `max_job_retries: 0` didn't stop retries","id":"setting-max_job_retries-0-didnt-stop-retries","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A configured ",["$","code",null,{"children":"0"}]," is read as unset and falls back to the default of ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"3"}],". The\nfield cannot express \"never retry\" through that field. If an action must not be\nretried, that has to be handled above Forge."]}]}],["$","$L59",null,{"title":"A long action fails with an invalid-argument error about timeouts","id":"a-long-action-fails-with-an-invalid-argument-error-about-timeouts","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"max_action_timeout_s"}]," on the worker defaults to ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"20 minutes"}],", and a client\nrequesting a longer timeout is ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"rejected outright"}]," rather than clamped down to\nthe maximum. Long link steps and EDA runs need this raised on the worker before\nthe client asks for it. (The field also accepts the older spelling\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_action_timeout"}],".)"]}]}],["$","$L59",null,{"title":"Workers exhaust file descriptors under load","id":"workers-exhaust-file-descriptors-under-load","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The process-wide open-file semaphore defaults to 24,576, which a worker running\nmany concurrent actions over a filesystem store will reach. Raise ","$L5a","\nunder ","$L5b",", and raise the OS ","$L5c"," limit to at least match; the\nsemaphore does not know what the kernel will allow."]}]}],"$L5d","$L5e"]}]
4d:["$","a",null,{"href":"/operate/scaling-cas","data-next-step":"next","className":"my-4 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 no-underline transition-colors border-brand/40 bg-brand-soft/30 hover:border-brand/70","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"18","height":"18","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-brand","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6"}]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-mono text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted-foreground","children":"Next"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-foreground","children":"Scaling the CAS"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"The other half of capacity: composing the store graph, sizing eviction, and\nwhy a second CAS process is harder than a second worker."}]}]]}]]}]
