56:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"workers"}]," returns every connected worker with what it registered, what it\nhas left after its running actions' reservations, its running count, its\npause and drain flags and the free memory it last reported. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"demand"}],"\nreturns every queued action with its operation id, when it was queued, its\npriority and its platform properties, reservations included. A worker's id\nstarts with the name it registered under, which on Kubernetes is the pod\nname, so a drain script can find the ids to drain from the pod."]}]
